    <h2 class="text-center page-title">

        ⏱️ Time and Work

    </h2>


    <hr>


    <!-- ==========================================
         INTRODUCTION
    =========================================== -->

    <p>

        Time and Work is an important quantitative aptitude
        topic used in placement examinations. It deals with
        the relationship between the amount of work, time
        required and efficiency of workers.

        These concepts are useful for solving questions
        involving individual work, combined work, efficiency,
        wages, pipes and cisterns.

    </p>


    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPICS COVERED
    =========================================== -->

    <h4 class="mt-4">

        📚 Topics Covered

    </h4>


    <ul class="list-group mb-4">

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Basic Work Concepts
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Work Efficiency
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Individual Work
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Combined Work
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Work and Wages
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Pipes and Cisterns
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Men, Women and Children Work
        </li>

        <li class="list-group-item">
            Work and Time Relationship
        </li>

    </ul>


    <!-- ==========================================
         TOPIC DEFINITIONS
    =========================================== -->

    <h4>

        📖 Topic Definitions

    </h4>


    <div class="accordion"
         id="timeWorkTopics">


        <!-- BASIC WORK -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#basicWork">

                    1. Basic Work Concept

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="basicWork"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Work represents the task completed by
                    a person or group.

                    <br><br>

                    If a person completes a work in 10 days,
                    then the work completed in one day is:

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>One Day's Work = 1 / Number of Days</strong>

                    <br><br>

                    Example:

                    <br>

                    If A completes a work in 10 days:

                    <br>

                    A's one-day work = 1/10.

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- EFFICIENCY -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#efficiency">

                    2. Work Efficiency

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="efficiency"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Efficiency represents how quickly a person
                    can complete a particular amount of work.

                    <br><br>

                    A person with higher efficiency completes
                    the same work in less time.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>Efficiency ∝ 1 / Time</strong>

                    <br><br>

                    Therefore, if A takes 10 days and B takes
                    5 days, B is twice as efficient as A.

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- INDIVIDUAL WORK -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#individualWork">

                    3. Individual Work

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="individualWork"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Individual work problems determine the
                    amount of work completed by one person.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>One Day's Work = 1 / Total Days</strong>

                    <br><br>

                    Example:

                    <br>

                    If A completes a job in 20 days:

                    <br>

                    A's one-day work = 1/20.

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- COMBINED WORK -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#combinedWork">

                    4. Combined Work

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="combinedWork"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Combined work means two or more people
                    work together to complete the same task.

                    <br><br>

                    Their individual work rates are added.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>
                        Combined Rate = A's Rate + B's Rate
                    </strong>

                    <br><br>

                    Example:

                    <br>

                    A completes work in 10 days and B
                    completes it in 20 days.

                    <br><br>

                    Combined rate:

                    <br>

                    1/10 + 1/20 = 3/20.

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- WORK AND WAGES -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#workWages">

                    5. Work and Wages

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="workWages"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Work and wages problems determine the
                    payment received by workers according
                    to the amount of work performed.

                    <br><br>

                    Wages are generally proportional to
                    the work done.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>
                        Wage Ratio = Work Ratio
                    </strong>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- PIPES -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#pipes">

                    6. Pipes and Cisterns

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="pipes"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    Pipes and cisterns problems involve
                    filling or emptying a tank using pipes.

                    <br><br>

                    A filling pipe adds water while an
                    emptying pipe removes water.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>
                        Net Rate = Filling Rate − Emptying Rate
                    </strong>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- MEN WOMEN CHILDREN -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#menWomen">

                    7. Men, Women and Children Work

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="menWomen"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    These problems compare the efficiency
                    of men, women and children.

                    <br><br>

                    If the efficiency ratio is known, the
                    amount of work performed can be compared.

                    <br><br>

                    Example:

                    <br>

                    If 2 men do the same work as 3 women:

                    <br>

                    <strong>
                        1 Man = 3/2 Women
                    </strong>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


        <!-- WORK TIME -->

        <div class="accordion-item">

            <h2 class="accordion-header">

                <button
                    class="accordion-button collapsed"
                    data-bs-toggle="collapse"
                    data-bs-target="#workTime">

                    8. Work and Time Relationship

                </button>

            </h2>


            <div
                id="workTime"
                class="accordion-collapse collapse">

                <div class="accordion-body">

                    For the same amount of work, time and
                    efficiency are inversely proportional.

                    <br><br>

                    <strong>
                        Work = Efficiency × Time
                    </strong>

                    <br><br>

                    Therefore:

                    <br>

                    <strong>
                        Time = Work / Efficiency
                    </strong>

                </div>

            </div>

        </div>


    </div>


